    - 
    - 
  exitDialoguesPassed:
    lastVerdict: 1
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - Go on then. Your story still has a few pages left.
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - "You\u2019re letting the ending inside. I hope you\u2019re ready."
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - It doesn't matter where you go. The ink is already dry.
  exitDialoguesQuarantined:
    lastVerdict: 2
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - A room without books. How very dull for us both.
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - You think a cage changes the plot? How charmingly naive.
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - Isolation is just a waiting room for the inevitable.
  exitDialoguesKilled:
    lastVerdict: 3
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - "A violent edit. I suppose that\u2019s one way to end it."
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - "You\u2019ve skipped straight to the epilogue. A shame."
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - "And so, the book is closed. I\u2019ll see you in the dark."
  quarantineExitLines:
  - A room without a window. How very on-the-nose.
  - You think the cage changes the story. It doesn't. But I appreciate the effort.
  - This chapter was always going to end this way. You simply turned the page.
  killExitLines:
  - "And so the author\u2019s hand strikes. Clean work, as endings go."
  - I saw this page coming long before you did. It reads exactly as expected.
  - "Don\u2019t feel guilty. This was always my last line."
