  introDialogue: {fileID: 11400000, guid: a860c39d3bee20a4dbf1652f7a813971, type: 2}
  questionResponses:
  - question: Where are you coming from?
    earlyDaysAnswer: The library. I was returning some books to the archive.
    midDaysAnswer: The east wing of the library. The ash was getting into the bindings.
    finalDaysAnswer: Nowhere in particular. The roads don't really matter anymore.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: Nowhere. I have not left this house in weeks. The books
      come to me now. I don't know how.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: The market. I buy bread every morning. The same baker.
      The same loaf. Very ordinary.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: The library. I was there all day. Organizing the archive.
      Nothing unusual. It was a very ordinary day.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: 
  - question: Have you been experiencing any strange symptoms lately?
    earlyDaysAnswer: No. Though I did dream something last night that I shouldn't
      have been able to know.
    midDaysAnswer: My hands feel cold. They've felt cold for weeks now. I think they
      know something I don't.
    finalDaysAnswer: Strange is relative. Everything feels exactly as I expected
      it would.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: No. I sleep dreamlessly. Always have. What you dream
      is just what you ate for dinner.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: My hands are warm. Both of them. Nothing is wrong. I don't
      know why everyone is so concerned.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: Nothing unusual at all. I feel quite well. The future
      holds no particular interest for me at the moment.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: 
  - question: Who do you live with?
    earlyDaysAnswer: No one. Books are better company.
    midDaysAnswer: The silence. It moved in about a month ago and hasn't left.
    finalDaysAnswer: No one now. The last one left when the sky changed colour.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: My daughter. She has been with me for years. She reads
      in the evenings. She is very quiet.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: My daughter. She has been staying since the winter. She
      is in the next room right now.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: My daughter. She would never leave me. She is still
      there when I come home. I know she is.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: 
  idleBarks:
    earlyDays:
    - You have interesting hands, officer. Very short lifeline.
    - I read the same page three times this morning. It said something different
      each time.
    - That window behind you. I would not stand so close to it.
    - The last three people who sat where you sit did not last the week. Just something
      I noticed.
    midDays:
    - You look tired. Sleep while you still dream things worth dreaming.
    - I would not touch the ink today. It has a different smell than yesterday.
    - Do you feel the city getting quieter? That is not a good sign, officer.
    finalDays:
    - Your ending is very close now. It reads quite peacefully, I assure you.
    - Do not look so worried. The last chapter always comes eventually.
    - I have already read past this part. You do not need to know what happens next.
    uncannyEarlyDays: []
    uncannyMidDays: []
    uncannyFinalDays: []
  IDNumber: 5569992
